part gen_4
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-4 · Amounts in a foreign currency. An amount in florens is converted at the Central Bank's mid rate FX-FLR of the last business day before the event's day (.1), each amount alone, rounded to whole orts half up (.2); a bank's own rate is never used under the law (.3)."
  note "fx_mid holds the gazette's FX-FLR rows, each in its own version known on its publication day and governing that one day (gazette from = to); the households read it at prev_business(add_days(d, -1), holidays) through a def's at (L §4.3). A day with no row is a hole (GEN-6 .2)."

source gen_4 "General Provisions Act, GEN-4 Amounts in a foreign currency (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input fx_mid: num DUK/FLR question "What is the Central Bank's mid rate FX-FLR for this day (GEN-4 .1, gazette FX-FLR)?"

version gen4_v1
  cite gen_4
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-06-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "GEN-4 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-06-01; governs every conversion the law requires."

